{"name":"City Tower","hex":"#aeaba5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"},{"term":"tower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall, narrow structure (significantly taller than it is wide, either standing alone or forming part of a larger structure.","A very tall open-framed structure on which communications devices are installed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be very tall; to reach a high height.","To be high or lofty; to soar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tower"}],"entries":[{"title":"City Tower, Manchester","blocks":[{"text":"City Tower is a 30-storey high-rise office building situated in the Piccadilly Gardens area of Manchester city centre, England. As of June 2026, it is the 25th-tallest building in Greater Manchester, with a roof height of 107 metres (351 ft). It is the second-tallest office building in Manchester after the CIS Tower, and the third-tallest outside London after CIS Tower and 103 Colmore Row in Birmingham."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Sunley_Tower%2C_Manchester.jpg/330px-Sunley_Tower%2C_Manchester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Tower%2C_Manchester"},{"title":"Post & Echo Building","blocks":[{"text":"The Post & Echo Building, now occupied by Sony Interactive Entertainment Europe and the Meliã Liverpool Hotel, is located at 95 Old Hall Street in Liverpool city centre, England, and formerly housed the headquarters of the Liverpool Echo and Daily Post newspapers. It is also known as Metropolitan House and as City Tower. It is an international style-style building that stands 73 metres (240 ft) tall with 18 storeys, making it the joint-tenth-tallest building in the city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Liverpool_Echo_building_13_March_2013_004_stitch.jpg/330px-Liverpool_Echo_building_13_March_2013_004_stitch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post_%26_Echo_Building"},{"title":"City Tower (Prague)","blocks":[{"text":"City Tower is the tallest skyscraper in Prague and in Bohemia, and the second tallest one in the Czech Republic standing on the Pankrác Plain with a height of 109 meters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/City_Tower_Praha_20080514.JPG/330px-City_Tower_Praha_20080514.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Tower_(Prague)"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Manchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG/120px-Manchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Manchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG/250px-Manchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Manchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG/120px-Manchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManchester_Portland_Street_New_York_Street_1107.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Piccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg/120px-Piccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Piccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg/250px-Piccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Piccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg/120px-Piccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiccadilly%2C_Manchester_skyline_on_a_grey_July_evening.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Praha_Pankrac.jpg/120px-Praha_Pankrac.jpg?utm_so